  "term": "Children’s Depression Inventory",
  "definition": "The Children’s Depression Inventory is an assessment tool used to measure the severity of depressive symptoms in children and adolescents. Research on its newer version suggests that the way its scores group together can differ across populations, so interpretation may need culture-specific validation.",
